0.overline {06} × 8.overline {3}

**Formula Used:**

Multiplication of repeating decimals

**Calculation:**

Let x = 0.overline {06}

Then, 100x = 6.overline {06}

⇒ 100x - x = 6.overline {06} - 0.overline {06}

⇒ 99x = 6

⇒ x = 6 / 99

⇒ x = 2 / 33

Let y = 8.overline {3}

Then, 10y = 83.overline {3}

⇒ 10y - y = 83.overline {3} - 8.overline {3}

⇒ 9y = 75

⇒ y = 75 / 9

⇒ y = 25 / 3

Now, multiply x and y:

x × y = (2 / 33) × (25 / 3)

⇒ (2 × 25) / (33 × 3)

⇒ 50 / 99

Convert 50 / 99 to decimal:

50 / 99 = 0.overline {50}

